1
00:00:00,06 --> 00:00:03,00
- [Instructor] Zustand is another state management solution

2
00:00:03,00 --> 00:00:04,03
with an atomic approach,

3
00:00:04,03 --> 00:00:06,02
also inspired by Recoil.

4
00:00:06,02 --> 00:00:08,02
It was developed by Jotai.

5
00:00:08,02 --> 00:00:09,07
This lesson introduces you

6
00:00:09,07 --> 00:00:13,08
to the Zustand State Management Library in React.

7
00:00:13,08 --> 00:00:15,09
Zustand means state in German.

8
00:00:15,09 --> 00:00:18,06
It is a lightweight and a simple state management solution

9
00:00:18,06 --> 00:00:22,04
with an API based on hooks, similar to the React API.

10
00:00:22,04 --> 00:00:24,07
So everything is going to feel very familiar,

11
00:00:24,07 --> 00:00:26,03
comfortable and easy.

12
00:00:26,03 --> 00:00:27,02
To create the store,

13
00:00:27,02 --> 00:00:29,05
you're going to first import the method create

14
00:00:29,05 --> 00:00:31,07
from the library Zustand.

15
00:00:31,07 --> 00:00:33,08
Then we create a hook for the store

16
00:00:33,08 --> 00:00:35,08
which is use bear store.

17
00:00:35,08 --> 00:00:37,06
Then we define a state

18
00:00:37,06 --> 00:00:40,09
with an initial state for the bears, which is set at zero.

19
00:00:40,09 --> 00:00:42,06
And we also define functions

20
00:00:42,06 --> 00:00:45,03
which are going to be used to carry over the data.

21
00:00:45,03 --> 00:00:47,05
Then the state is bound to components.

22
00:00:47,05 --> 00:00:50,07
We're going to import the hook in our components

23
00:00:50,07 --> 00:00:53,08
and then bind the state to our components.

24
00:00:53,08 --> 00:00:54,06
That's it.

25
00:00:54,06 --> 00:00:57,01
This is a very simple data flow to manage it all.

26
00:00:57,01 --> 00:01:03,01
So let's check it out with an example.

27
00:01:03,01 --> 00:01:05,01
So in this sandbox we have a store.

28
00:01:05,01 --> 00:01:07,06
So this one is named use store

29
00:01:07,06 --> 00:01:10,02
and we define an initial state for the count

30
00:01:10,02 --> 00:01:13,08
which is set at one, and we also have a function

31
00:01:13,08 --> 00:01:16,08
that we're going to use to increment this value.

32
00:01:16,08 --> 00:01:19,07
Then inside the functional component, we bound the state.

33
00:01:19,07 --> 00:01:23,02
We bound the state to the store by calling use store,

34
00:01:23,02 --> 00:01:25,09
which is our base hook store.

35
00:01:25,09 --> 00:01:29,03
Then we can display the value of the count

36
00:01:29,03 --> 00:01:31,00
to display the value of the counter

37
00:01:31,00 --> 00:01:32,03
and also use inc,

38
00:01:32,03 --> 00:01:35,04
which is the function that we use to increment the value

39
00:01:35,04 --> 00:01:37,09
every time that you click on the button.

40
00:01:37,09 --> 00:01:39,08
So why choose Zustand

41
00:01:39,08 --> 00:01:43,08
over the Context API or Redux, for example?

42
00:01:43,08 --> 00:01:46,05
Well, first it requires less boilerplate code.

43
00:01:46,05 --> 00:01:48,03
Also, the data flow is very simple.

44
00:01:48,03 --> 00:01:51,02
With a simple hook, the store hook can be used everywhere

45
00:01:51,02 --> 00:01:54,07
from any components and no context provider is needed.

46
00:01:54,07 --> 00:01:57,01
So that is many reasons to choose Zustand

47
00:01:57,01 --> 00:01:58,09
as a state management solution.

48
00:01:58,09 --> 00:02:01,08
In these sections, the project will build our (indistinct)

49
00:02:01,08 --> 00:02:05,00
and a checklist for the challenge parts at the end.

50
00:02:05,00 --> 00:02:06,05
So let's see how to use Zustand

51
00:02:06,05 --> 00:02:08,00
as a state management solution.

